statement:
Return `true` if the pattern `p` matches the whole string `s`, and `false` otherwise. Inside the pattern:

- a lowercase letter stands for exactly that letter;
- `?` stands for exactly one character, whatever it is;
- `*` stands for any run of characters, of any length including zero.

The match must use up all of `s` from its first character to its last; matching just a piece of `s` is not enough.

validator:
function validate([s, p]) {
  if (typeof s !== 'string' || typeof p !== 'string') return 's and p must be strings.';
  if (s.length > 2000 || p.length > 2000) return 's and p have at most 2000 characters each.';
  if (!/^[a-z]*$/.test(s)) return 's contains only lowercase letters.';
  if (!/^[a-z?*]*$/.test(p)) return "p contains only lowercase letters, '?' and '*'.";
  return null;
}

